# Project Structure and Entry Points

The app uses Next.js App Router with TypeScript.

- Main app entry: [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx) and [src/app/page.tsx](mdc:src/app/page.tsx)
- Global styles: [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css)
- Next.js config: [next.config.ts](mdc:next.config.ts)
- TypeScript config: [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) (alias `@/*` → `src/*`)
- ESLint config: [eslint.config.mjs](mdc:eslint.config.mjs)
- PostCSS (Tailwind v4): [postcss.config.mjs](mdc:postcss.config.mjs)

Conventions:
- Use the App Router. Route segments live under `src/app/*`.
- Co-locate domain modules under `src/*`; import with `@/...` based on `paths`.
- Keep server-only code out of client components; annotate with `"use client"` only when needed.
